{
  "_about": "Output-language strings and per-language verification vocabulary for the LLM explanation layer. A simple JSON dict, deliberately not an i18n framework.",
  "_why_verification_vocab_lives_here": "The guard that checks generated text has to know, per language, what a finding-style assertion looks like and what counts as historical elaboration. Those lists are language data, not logic, so they live beside the prompt strings and can be extended without touching code.",
  "_bias": "Every list here is written to over-reject rather than under-reject. A rejected explanation costs nothing — the deterministic rule_statement is always present — whereas one hallucinated detail is enough for an institution to distrust and discard the tool.",
